-- ── 10 Alerts ────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- ── 10 Suppliers (SUPPLIER_PROFILE) ─────────────────────────
-- quality_score is stored as a defect rate (lower is better) and
-- responsiveness_score on a 1-10 scale (see SupplierScorecardDto, which
-- does `100 - qualityScore` and `responsivenessScore * 10` when building
-- the display scorecard). The values below are that conversion applied to
-- the intended 0-100 "higher is better" quality/responsiveness scores
-- (e.g. SUPP-001 is meant to read as quality 88, responsiveness 95).

-- ── Supplier Delivery History (SUPPLIER_DELIVERY) — BB-SUP-03 ──
-- On-time ratio per supplier tuned to match that supplier's SUPPLIER_PROFILE.tier
-- above (PREFERRED>=95%, APPROVED>=85%, CONDITIONAL>=70%, PROBATION<70% — see
-- SupplierService.tierFromOtd). Without this, otdScore/atRisk in the live scorecard
-- (computed from this table) never matched the seeded tier at all.

-- ── Supplier Dependency Graph (SUPPLIER_DEPENDENCY) ──────────
-- A small, real (2-3 tier) dependency chain among the suppliers already
-- seeded above, so /api/suppliers/{id}/cascaded-risk and /structural-risk
-- are demoable without extra setup:
--   Delta Electronics India (SUPP-005, our one at-risk supplier) is the
--   sole source of connector housings for Taiwan Semiconductors (SUPP-003),
--   which in turn feeds silicon wafers to Infineon (SUPP-009) -- a 2-hop
--   chain to exercise decay. Foxconn/Shenzhen is a separate, non-critical,
--   non-sole-source edge for contrast.

-- ── Supplier ESG Profiles (SUPPLIER_ESG_PROFILE) ─────────────
-- Deliberately incomplete, matching the plan's own note that most
-- suppliers won't have ESG data initially: SUPP-001 has a full profile,
-- SUPP-005 (Delta) has 2 compliance violations -- exercising the
-- esg_compliance_review action suggestion, SUPP-003 has partial data
-- (missing compliance/labor), and every other supplier has no row at all
-- (esg-risk correctly reports "no data" for them, not a fabricated score).

